              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Latin for unmarried, then the Latin for rainy."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: paucī, paucae, pauca",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "paucī, paucae, pauca — \"few\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "paucī is the plural of paucus, \"few\" (Lewis & Short), usually traced to Proto-Indo-European peh2w-, \"few, small\" (EtymDB 2.1); English few is a cousin."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
